      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dragon2439/{size}/2230_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-03T02:53:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"krysskroz\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/a88e4f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> krysskroz:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Went with Dragon Shield Clear Standard.&nbsp; I found a dealer on Ebay that was willing to sell them for a few bucks less than retail since I was buying 15 packs.&nbsp; I am about 1/2 way done and I have not had a single imperfect sleeve, and I know Dragon lasts very well.&nbsp; I just need to get a 2nd Rook/Infernal box so that they all fit.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Dragon shields are the best sleeves for cards (imo). Ive been using them for years and have only had a few wear out on me. The only real problem with them is price, and it was expensive to sleeve this entire game in them. They also take up more space, as do all sleeves.&nbsp;</p>",
